A||N||8||85gt||Speaker question||||10||
Z||000000||85gt||01-27-2001||07:56 PM||||I have a 85 and was wondering if you could put rear speakers like the ones in the 86 in it. I want to leave the headrest speakers. I'm trying to get a real good sound, without having to build boxes.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Alex2004||01-27-2001||08:30 PM||||We did that to my 84 SE.  You have to cut through the metal though real carefully so you don't break the glass. You will need some sort of metal cutting tool, the side panel off of 86 + fiero, but be sure the get the plastic speaker mounts!  Hope that helps any.  The first speaker we installed took about 3 hours to do since we didn't really know where to start, the second time we did it, it was about an hour. e-mail me if you have any other questions about it.  <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A>  or instant message me on MSN with that hotmail address, or IM me on AOL, my screen name is AbercrombieAlex6 <P>Alex||||reg||1
Z||000002||JasonC||01-27-2001||11:56 PM||||Do you have some pics of the install? That's basically all I'v been thinking about doing to my system since I got the car. In the pillars and in the doors(maybe). I think the headreast thing is too close and won't give good imaging. Those 2 4x10's just don't cut it for me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jason Carmichael<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-r.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.getpaid2surf.net/97GPGT" TARGET=_blank>My GP GT on the net.</A> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-l.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||RiceCooker||01-28-2001||12:52 PM||||Just my opinion, but I think the 4x6's in the sail panel are not very good at all.<P>They face the middle of the car and they're behind the seat. No matter how i balanced the front/rear (with the stock speaker locations) i just didn't seem to be able to achieve a good sound or balance.<P>What I'm trying to say is that if you're putting in a lot of time and effort, there are better things you can do. Now I don't have many suggestions and I'm no sound expert, but I think in the spring I will experiment with building 5 1/4" speaker placements in the sail panel corners. Some people have built 6x9 boxes up there as well.<BR>Other options include subs behind seats, 6x9's in doors, etc.  <P>Just my $0.02<BR>What does everyone else think of the 4x6's?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||01-28-2001||01:03 PM||||i've only recently got a fiero with the seat speakers (had my '87 about3 years. just got a couple of '84's last year). i kind of like them, i just don't expect a lot out of them. i've got the fader down to the point where i barely hear them. situated as they are and adjusted it's actually a good rearfill location. a bit of delay some how might make it perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-28-2001||01:26 PM||||I don't like the sound of a 4 X 6 speaker. That is why I am installing a set of 4" component speakers in the sails. I am also installing a digital surround sound processor so I can adjust the level and delay to the speakers. This will keep my stage set to the front and use the back as a delayed fill. When I'm done it will sound like a stereo in a large car. Staged to the front and seperation should be excellent. (I have heard this type of set-up in other cars and it sounded great.)<BR>There are pics of the tweeters in another thread. I am almost done with the woofers for the sails. When done I'll post pic's.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||01-28-2001||01:41 PM||||I don't have any pics yets. But i am going to install my 3rd brake light probably today so i will take the panels off and get some pics.  It might be alittle while before they are developed but i'll post a topic or something if it is to long ok.  TTYL<P>Alex.<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000007||batboy||01-30-2001||04:37 PM||||85GT, people have used the 4X6 speakers in older Fieros mainly to make it look like a factory install. I've looked into adding speakers on my 85 too. Looks like a pair of round 4" (with grills) would fit better than the 4X6's and probably sound as good if not better.. You can get component mids and tweets in this size too (like Infinity Kappa 40.2cs, etc.)||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||01-30-2001||08:09 PM||||if you're going to put some 4x6s back there, i would recommend you get some that have a swiveling tweeter. that way you can aim it more towards the front. i tried 4x6s with and without the swivel tweeter, and it definately makes a difference.<BR>i'm probably gonna end up going with some 4x6 plates or do a setup like oreif's.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
